      {
        "company": "ROAR Organic",
        "description": "<p><strong>Job Title: </strong></p><p>Area Sales Manager</p><p><strong>Reports to:</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Director of Sales- East</p><p><strong>Location:</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Remote- New York Metro</p><p><strong>Status:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p>FT/Exempt</p><p><strong>Compensation:</strong></p><p>$70,000 â $80,000 annual base salary, plus a competitive bonus opportunity. Final compensation will be commensurate with experience, skills, and qualifications.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>ABOUT THE COMPANY</strong></p><p>ROAR is redefining hydration for a new generation. In a category that has become overly serious and hardcore performance obsessed, ROAR stands for something different: hydration that is expressive, effortless, and rooted in real life. Built for people who move, connect, and live life out loud, ROAR delivers complete hydration with vitamins, antioxidants, and electrolytes - all with just 20 calories and 3g of sugar or less per bottle.</p><p><br></p><p>More than a beverage, ROAR is a cultural signal - bright, approachable, and fun. It rejects the intensity and rules of traditional hydration in favor of something more human: joy, spontaneity, and the kind of movement that doesnât need a scoreboard. This positioning has resonated with consumers and retailers alike driving strong momentum across both natural and conventional retail, where ROAR continues to expand rapidly and now ranks as the #2 brand in the natural channel within the enhanced water category.</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>ROLE OVERVIEW</strong></p><p>ROAR Organic is seeking a hands-on Sales Leader to drive profitable growth in a fast-paced, high-growth environment. This role is responsible for leading all sales activities across grocery customers in the New York Metro area, including new business development, key account management, and executing data-driven strategies to expand market share and increase brand awareness.</p><p><br></p><p>The ideal candidate brings a proven track record of scaling high-growth brands profitably, with experience managing both established and emerging grocery retailers, as well as partners. They are highly relationship-driven, resourceful, and action-oriented, with strong communication and organizational skills. This leader excels at building and implementing the strategies, tools, and processes needed to support sustained growth.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES</strong></p><ul><li>Deliver against Annual Operating Plan targets, including gross/net sales and trade spend objectives.</li><li>Grow distribution and topline revenue with a focus on regional and independent retailers.</li><li>Execute customer sales strategies, promotional calendars, and account plans.</li><li>Leverage distributer incentive programs and independent retailer promotional opportunities to drive sales.</li><li>Conduct weekly route rides with distributor sales representatives to support execution and identify growth opportunities.</li><li>Develop and own a field execution strategy based on weekly trend reports, promotional planners, and merchandising opportunities.</li><li>Manage and execute trade spend programs to drive profitable growth and promotional effectiveness.</li><li>Leverage syndicated data (IRI, SPINS) to communicate compelling, retailer-specific presentations.</li><li>Track, measure, and analyze performance metrics, including ROI.</li><li>Represent the brand at regional and national trade shows, customer meetings, and industry events.</li></ul><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>SKILLS &amp; EXPERIENCE</strong></p><ul><li>Minimum 2 years of CPG sales experience.</li><li>Strong understanding of the beverage and grocery landscape, including retailers and distributors.</li><li>Experience executing sales planning initiatives.</li><li>Creative, solutions-oriented problem solver with a strong sense of ownership and accountability.</li><li>Thrives in a hands-on, fast-paced, entrepreneurial environment.</li><li>Proficient in Microsoft Excel and PowerPoint; experience with syndicated data tools (SPINS, IRI) preferred.</li><li>Ability to travel extensively as needed.</li><li>Ability to stand and walk for extended periods.</li><li>Ability to lift up to 30 pounds.</li><li>Must be authorized to work in the U.S. without current or future sponsorship.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><br/><br/>Please mention the word **STIRRINGLY** and tag RMTIuMjQ4LjEzMy4yNDI= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMTIuMjQ4LjEzMy4yNDI=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.",
